cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use microGEM, please cite this file."
type: software
title: "microGEM: sequence-based scoring of 17 microbial enzyme chemistries with an explicitly calibrated, distribution-ready classifier"
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Jun
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/xGroup5/microgem"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xGroup5/microgem"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  microGEM scores uncharacterised microbial proteins against seventeen enzyme
  chemistries relevant to mucosal biology, using a frozen ESM-2 650M embedding
  and one calibrated linear probe per panel. The package reports per-panel
  reliability tiers, prevalence-adjusted precision and a decision margin, and
  ships with an installation self-test.
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - enzyme function prediction
  - protein language model
  - ESM-2
  - calibration
  - microbiome
